---
// src/pages/how-we-work.astro — Commercial Model & Operating Process
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="How We Work — Commercial Model & Sourcing Process"
  description="Learn how InfraHub understands requirements, evaluates suitable approaches, introduces specialist providers, and separates advisory from partner delivery."
  canonicalPath="/how-we-work"
>
  <div class="work-page-wrapper">
    <div class="container work-container">
      
      <!-- Left-aligned Editorial Header -->
      <header class="work-header">
        <span class="work-kicker">How the model works</span>
        <h1 class="work-title">How InfraHub Works</h1>
        <p class="work-lead">
          A four-stage process for turning a technical requirement into a qualified provider conversation without pretending every service is delivered by InfraHub.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- 4 Stages Timeline (Clean Architectural Design) -->
      <section class="stages-timeline">
        <div class="stage-block">
          <div class="stage-index-col">
            <span class="stage-mono-num">01</span>
            <div class="stage-vertical-line"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-main-col">
            <span class="stage-kicker">Understand</span>
            <h2 class="stage-headline">Understand the Requirement</h2>
            <p class="stage-narrative">
              We start with the requirement rather than a vendor catalog. The detail depends on the project, but the first pass usually establishes:
            </p>
            <ul class="stage-specs-list">
              <li><strong>Traffic Profiles:</strong> Inbound-heavy, egress-intensive, or balanced eyeball peering.</li>
              <li><strong>Resilience Requirements:</strong> Redundancy, physical diversity, recovery expectations, support boundaries, and failure scenarios.</li>
              <li><strong>Commercial Scope:</strong> Port or capacity commitments, installation costs, cross-connects, term, support, and expected growth.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="stage-block">
          <div class="stage-index-col">
            <span class="stage-mono-num">02</span>
            <div class="stage-vertical-line"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-main-col">
            <span class="stage-kicker">Match</span>
            <h2 class="stage-headline">Evaluate &amp; Match Suitable Options</h2>
            <p class="stage-narrative">
              InfraHub compares relevant providers and approaches against the technical, geographic, operational, and commercial requirements. Where resilience matters, the comparison should distinguish provider diversity from actual physical-path evidence.
            </p>
            <ul class="stage-specs-list">
              <li><strong>Network Fit:</strong> Routing, peering, upstreams, traffic profile, and the provider's presence in the required markets.</li>
              <li><strong>Physical Presence:</strong> Facility availability, interconnection path, building entry, and route evidence where those details affect the design.</li>
              <li><strong>Commercial Fit:</strong> Recurring and one-time charges, contract term, billing model, support, and provider-specific conditions.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="stage-block">
          <div class="stage-index-col">
            <span class="stage-mono-num">03</span>
            <div class="stage-vertical-line"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-main-col">
            <span class="stage-kicker">Introduce</span>
            <h2 class="stage-headline">Direct Specialist Introduction</h2>
            <p class="stage-narrative">
              When a partner-delivered service is the right path, InfraHub coordinates an introduction to the selected provider so technical questions, availability, pricing, and delivery responsibilities can be confirmed directly.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="stage-block">
          <div class="stage-index-col">
            <span class="stage-mono-num">04</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-main-col">
            <span class="stage-kicker">Deliver</span>
            <h2 class="stage-headline">Direct Contracting & Ongoing Operations</h2>
            <p class="stage-narrative">
              For partner-delivered services, the selected specialist confirms the applicable contract, service commitments, implementation, and ongoing delivery. InfraHub can remain involved in qualification, coordination, renewals, or future sourcing where useful.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Commercial FAQ (Editorial Broadside) -->
      <section class="work-faq-section">
        <div class="faq-header">
          <span class="faq-kicker">Commercial questions</span>
          <h2 class="faq-headline">Frequently Asked Commercial Questions</h2>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-accordion-list">
          <div class="faq-entry">
            <h3 class="faq-question">How is InfraHub involved commercially?</h3>
            <p class="faq-answer">
              InfraHub's role depends on the engagement. For partner-delivered services, provider pricing and contracting are confirmed directly with the selected provider. Any separate InfraHub commercial arrangement should be made clear before the engagement proceeds.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-entry">
            <h3 class="faq-question">Why wouldn't an engineering team just contact the carrier directly?</h3>
            <p class="faq-answer">
              You can. InfraHub is most useful when the requirement needs comparison across more than one provider, technology, location, or commercial model. The goal is to define the requirement first and then evaluate which options deserve a direct provider conversation.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-entry">
            <h3 class="faq-question">Who holds the contractual relationship and SLA?</h3>
            <p class="faq-answer">
              For partner-delivered services such as IP transit, optical wavelengths, cloud, DDoS protection, or managed operations, contracting, billing, and service commitments are agreed directly with the selected provider under that provider's applicable terms. Direct hardware sourcing may be quoted by InfraHub or handled through the applicable supplier arrangement, depending on the transaction.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Footer CTA -->
      <div class="work-footer-cta">
        <h2 class="cta-headline">Ready to evaluate your infrastructure requirements?</h2>
        <p class="cta-desc">Discuss your throughput, latency, and hardware constraints with an infrastructure advisor.</p>
        <div class="cta-actions">
          <a href="/lets-talk" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Start a Sourcing Conversation</a>
          <a href="/solutions/infrastructure" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">Explore Solutions</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .work-page-wrapper {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    padding: 64px 0 96px;
  }
  .work-container {
    max-width: 1040px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 72px;
  }

  /* Left-aligned Editorial Header */
  .work-header {
    max-width: 860px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }
  .work-kicker {
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    }
  .work-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 4.5vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .work-lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  /* Architectural Timeline */
  .stages-timeline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .stage-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .stage-index-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .stage-mono-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    padding: 6px 0;
  }
  .stage-vertical-line {
    width: 1px;
    background-color: var(--border-color);
    flex-grow: 1;
    margin: 8px 0;
  }
  .stage-main-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    padding-bottom: 48px;
  }
  .stage-kicker {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    }
  .stage-headline {
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .stage-narrative {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .stage-specs-list {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .stage-specs-list strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  /* FAQ Section */
  .work-faq-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 28px;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }
  .faq-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .faq-kicker {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    }
  .faq-headline {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.3rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .faq-accordion-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .faq-entry {
    padding: 28px 32px;
    background-color: #ffffff;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .faq-entry:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .faq-question {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .faq-answer {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Footer CTA */
  .work-footer-cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    padding-top: 32px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }
  .cta-headline {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .cta-desc {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 680px;
  }
  .cta-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
</style>
